From 34fa88792d43ccfb1ee24544694d77b8577af70b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 08:45:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Listings from agents and managers wait for an admin to
 publish
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Anyone who is not an admin now proposes a listing rather than
publishing one. It is saved with approval='pending' and stays out of
the listings page, the global search, the stale-listings screen, the
dashboard counts and both exports until an admin publishes it. The
author still sees it, so they can follow it and correct it.

Rejecting sends it back with a note explaining what to change, which
reaches the author as a notification and shows on the listing itself.
They fix it and resubmit. A note is required — sending work back
without saying why is how people stop bothering.

Approval is a separate column from status on purpose: status is about
the market, and a listing waiting to be published still needs to be
Available or Reserved. Existing rows default to 'approved' so the 171
listings already in the database stay live through the upgrade.

Editing an already-published listing still takes effect immediately;
only new listings wait.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01U3sgXu7uGRzpkyQXbzW1dC
